rently limited to small and domain-specific scenarios — to ensure the validity of generated triplets, schema informa- tion (e.g., possible entity and relation types) has to be included in the prompt."},{"id":"c4","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_7838b27d7f75411d","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":9,"quote":"Rebel: Relation extraction by end-to-end language generation."},{"id":"c5","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_38470e14d01b3cab","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":7,"quote":"For example, the information that connects the knowledge graph and the query \"Who is Justin Bieber’s brother?\" is not a specific passage but instead the entity \"Justin Bieber\" and the relation \"brother of\"."},{"id":"c6","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_bf4567b8222087fb","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":24,"quote":"• Relation Extraction: Relation extraction aims to extract semantic relationships between entities in text, which often requires local, global, syntactic, and semantic dependencies, especially in the case of document-level relation"},{"id":"c7","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_690d7ef285bc963c","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":17,"quote":"• Edge list: The edge list represents each edge in the graph, typically in the form of tuples or triples, such as (i, j) or (i, r, j), where i and j are nodes, and r is the relation between nodes i and j."},{"id":"c8","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_5378afbd1af02420","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":7,"quote":"• Redundancy: We employ a redundancy score — the average cosine similarity among each canonicalized relation and its nearest coun- terpart — where low scores indicate that the schema’s relations are semantically distinct."},{"id":"c9","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_65376575c9d615eb","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":3,"quote":"Through few-shot prompt- ing, LLMs identify and extract relational triplets ([Subject, Relation, Object]) from input texts, inde- pendent of any specific schema."},{"id":"c10","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_e104895593a4fe3c","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":11,"quote":"Revisiting relation extraction in the era of large language models."},{"id":"c11","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_fb198057dee65e19","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":21,"quote":"Given the set of k relations, for each sub-sentence, they retrieve all triples that contain a relation in Ri,k and whose entities are in S i∈I Si."},{"id":"c12","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_efa9451554fb14fe","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":1,"quote":"n’ Can the relation ‘participatedIn’ be replaced by ‘mission’ given the current context?"},{"id":"c13","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_c7c4761d7fb96ad6","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":5,"quote":"We then finetune the embedding model to distin- guish between the correct relation associated with a given text and other non-relevant relations using the InfoNCE loss."},{"id":"c14","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_7838b27d7f75411d","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":9,"quote":"Neural relation extraction for knowledge base enrichment."},{"id":"c15","chunkId":"01d8